      "supported": 0.60,
      "rejected": 0.03,
      "untestable": 0.05,
      "artifact": 0.07,
      "uncertain": 0.25
    },
    "decision": "proceed_with_changes",
    "design": {
      "estimand": "The causal effect of a team's offensive play type X on the opponent's immediate next-possession points per possession, defined as the difference in expected opponent PPP following a possession of type X relative to following a possession of any other type, controlling for context.",
      "unit": "A paired sequence: Team A offensive possession with recorded play type X, followed by the very next offensive possession by Team B (opponent).",
      "sample": "All such paired possessions from NBA regular season and playoffs, 2022-23 through 2025-26. Exclude possessions where: (a) the play type is OTHER (due to known foul-artifact severity); (b) the possession ends a period, leaving no opponent possession; (c) garbage time (last 5 min of 4th quarter with score differential > 20). The primary analysis pools all seasons; a season-by-season sensitivity check will be performed.",
      "power": "Pooled across seasons, expected N per play type (using SF07 rates) ranges from ~23,500 (PUTBACK) to ~230,000 (DRIVE). To detect a +0.05 PPP effect at 80% power and α=0.05 (two-sided) with a standard deviation of ~0.4 (typical possession-level PPP), the smallest type requires ~1,568 samplings per group; PUTBACK's roughly half that may be borderline. We will report effect sizes with 95% CIs for all types; pre-register that only types with lower confidence bound exceeding +0.10 opponent PPP (the AVOID threshold) will be flagged.",
      "controls": "Fixed effects: own team, opponent team, home/away, period, score margin (binned), back-to-back indicator, rest days. Lineup quality: on-court net rating (or pre-game season-to-date net rating) of both the own defensive unit and the opponent offensive unit. Also include a lagged term: opponent's PPP in the immediately preceding possession (their possession before our play type X) to control for their recent offensive efficiency. For own-sequence lag analysis, add factors for lag-1 play type and PPP of the own team.",
